__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.cache/
.r2g/
# The build lock sits *beside* the output directory, not inside it -- for
# `-o .r2g` that is `..r2g.r2glock` in the repo root, so `.r2g/` does not cover
# it. Normally unlinked on exit; it only lingers after a crashed build, which
# is exactly when an unexplained untracked file is least welcome.
*.r2glock
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
out/
# Generated by CI from uv.lock (uv export); never committed.
requirements-ci.txt
requirements-rag.txt
# Agent run logs. The CHANGELOG's `### Removed` entry has claimed these were
# "now gitignored" since they were deleted from the tree, but no rule actually
# matched them -- so nothing stopped a re-run dropping them straight back in.
# Anchored and path-specific on purpose: `.github/remediation-tracking.md` is a
# deliberate, committed planning doc, and a bare `remediation-tracking.md`
# pattern would swallow it.
/DONE.md
/docs/BUILD_STATE*.md
/docs/remediation-tracking.md
